%% APX AutoMai — Level 1 Data Flow Diagram
flowchart TB
    GUEST[Guest]
    CUST[Customer]
    ADMIN[Administrator]
    CRON[External Cron Service]
    MAIL[Email Service]
    SMSG[SMS Gateway]

    P1["1.0<br/>Authentication and<br/>Role-Based Access"]
    P2["2.0<br/>Vehicle<br/>Management"]
    P3["3.0<br/>Booking and<br/>Scheduling"]
    P4["4.0<br/>Booking<br/>Management"]
    P5["5.0<br/>Appointment<br/>Reminders"]
    P8["8.0<br/>Maintenance Due<br/>Detection"]
    P6["6.0<br/>Loyalty<br/>Points"]
    P7["7.0<br/>Reporting and<br/>Dashboard"]

    D1[(D1 users / customers)]
    D2[(D2 vehicles)]
    D3[(D3 services / bundles)]
    D4[(D4 bookings + booking_service)]
    D5[(D5 loyalty_ledger)]
    D6[(D6 audit_logs)]
    D7[(D7 sms_logs)]
    D8[(D8 settings + message templates)]
    D9[(D9 maintenance_rules)]
    D10[(D10 reminders)]

    CUST -->|credentials| P1
    ADMIN -->|credentials| P1
    P1 <-->|account record, role| D1
    P1 -->|session for role| CUST
    P1 -->|session for role| ADMIN

    CUST -->|vehicle details, optional mileage| P2
    P2 <-->|vehicle record| D2

    GUEST -->|guest booking| P3
    CUST -->|service or bundle, date, time, points to use| P3
    P3 -->|read catalogue and prices| D3
    P3 -->|read capacity and hours| D8
    P3 -->|check existing slots| D4
    P3 -->|save booking and price snapshots| D4
    P3 -->|read owned vehicle| D2
    P3 -->|deduct points| P6
    P3 -->|reference number| CUST
    P3 -->|reference number| GUEST
    P3 -->|booking received email| MAIL

    ADMIN -->|confirm, complete, cancel, assign mechanic| P4
    P4 <-->|booking record| D4
    P4 -->|who, what, why| D6
    P4 -->|award or reverse points| P6
    P4 -->|status change notice| MAIL
    P4 -->|stamp last service date and mileage| D2

    %% 5.0 — you have an appointment coming up.
    CRON -->|scheduled tick| P5
    P5 -->|find confirmed bookings in window| D4
    P5 -->|read template and triggers| D8
    P5 -->|read contact details| D1
    P5 -->|claim before sending, exactly once| D10
    P5 -->|send email| MAIL
    P5 -->|send SMS| SMSG
    P5 -->|record every attempt| D7

    %% 8.0 — your vehicle is due for servicing. Nothing the customer did
    %% triggers this; only the passage of time, which is why it is scheduled.
    CRON -->|scheduled tick| P8
    P8 -->|read service intervals| D9
    P8 -->|read last service date and mileage| D2
    P8 -->|skip if work already booked| D4
    P8 -->|read template and triggers| D8
    P8 -->|claim once per interval| D10
    P8 -->|service due email| MAIL
    P8 -->|service due SMS| SMSG
    P8 -->|record every attempt| D7
    ADMIN -->|edit intervals and templates| D8

    %% The dashboard runs the same due calculation, so the screen and the
    %% inbox cannot disagree about whether a car is due.
    P8 -->|due status per vehicle| CUST

    P6 <-->|earn, redeem, expire, adjust| D5
    P6 -->|balance and history| CUST
    ADMIN -->|manual adjustment with reason| P6
    P6 -->|adjustment record| D6

    ADMIN -->|date range filter| P7
    P7 -->|completed work and snapshots| D4
    P7 -->|outstanding points liability| D5
    P7 -->|scheduler heartbeat| D8
    P7 -->|figures and charts| ADMIN
